window.docContents[215].resolve({"/#The-Riemann-proof-structure--Analytic-reductions":{"contents":"Claim.factor_ne_zeroA removed prime Euler factor cannot vanish when the real part is positive.Original declaration, line 7\n\nClaim.prim_zeroA zero in the open strip descends to the primitive character after removing the nonvanishing Euler factors.Original declaration, line 23\n\nLine 33 uses factor_ne_zero.\n\nClaim.gamma_ne_zeroThe character gamma factor is nonzero in the open right half-plane.Original declaration, line 35\n\nClaim.prim_reflectReflects a primitive zero to the inverse character at one minus the original point by the completed functional equation.Original declaration, line 42\n\nLine 51 uses gamma_ne_zero.\n\nClaim.stripFor a zero left of the critical line, descend to the primitive character and reflect it into the zero-free half-plane. Right-side zeros are excluded directly.Original declaration, line 59\n\nLine 67 uses prim_zero. Line 68 uses prim_reflect.\n\nClaim.zetaUses the level-one instance of the strip result and the zeta functional equation outside the strip. This is a component of the conjunction used by an export.Original declaration, line 75\n\nLine 82 uses strip.\n\nFormalism.VW.gammaFactor_ne_zeroProves gamma-factor nonvanishing in the separate primitive-character reduction.Original declaration, line 6\n\nFormalism.VW.critLineReflects a primitive Dirichlet zero and applies the half-plane hypothesis. This is the reduction used by the original primitive export.Original declaration, line 11\n\nLine 21 uses gammaFactor_ne_zero.\n\nFormalism.VW.rh_of_rightReflects a nontrivial zeta zero to show that right-half-plane nonvanishing forces real part one half.Original declaration, line 5\n\nFormalism.VW.rh_of_everySpecializes all-character nonvanishing to the trivial character at level one, identifies its L-function with zeta, and applies reflection.Original declaration, line 29\n\nLine 30 uses rh_of_right.\n\n","context":"The Riemann proof structure","header":"5. Analytic reductions","id":"/#The-Riemann-proof-structure--Analytic-reductions"}});